  "findings": [
    "The common allocator grants VMA access to the process DRM object, but the CWSR helper does not return its offset. The possible offset-discovery gap was followed into the retained GEM/VM/debugfs/fdinfo status implementation.",
    "amdgpu_gem_info iterates DRM object handles and prints size, placement, pin count, import/export inode, flags, and fences through amdgpu_bo_print_info. This function does not print the BO mmap offset.",
    "amdgpu_vm_info uses the same amdgpu_bo_print_info routine for BO status lists. Its displayed IDs are status-list ordinals; they are not a returned CWSR GEM handle or mmap offset.",
    "DRM fdinfo reports the PASID, aggregate memory statistics, and engine usage. It does not expose CWSR buffer offsets.",
    "These source paths provide no supported offset-discovery route for the internal CWSR allocation. The scope remains these interfaces; no guessed-offset scanning, endpoint accesses, or memory mappings were attempted."
  ],
